questions.passage_md:
A student removes a ring of bark about 2 cm wide, down to the wood, from a young branch of a guava plant. The ring cuts through the phloem but leaves the wood, which contains the xylem, untouched. After three weeks the student notes that:

- the bark just above the ring has swollen;
- the leaves above the ring are still green and fresh;
- the bark just below the ring has not swollen.
